      <memberdef kind="function" id="classService_1ac5c73e3e8d87d1a87af5c12dcee32013" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::optional&lt; std::string &gt;</type>
        <definition>static std::optional&lt; std::string &gt; Service::getServicePermissionsQuery</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;service_name, std::uint64_t service_id)</argsstring>
        <name>getServicePermissionsQuery</name>
        <qualifiedname>Service::getServicePermissionsQuery</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>service_name</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::uint64_t</type>
          <declname>service_id</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Builds the permission lookup for a service row by id. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns the owner/admin/staff columns used by <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> to authorise service-level actions. The table name and id are formatted into the query text rather than bound; the resulting text also serves as the permission cache key. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">service_name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Name of the service/organisation table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">service_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Primary key of the service row. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A SELECT statement (always produced by this implementation). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="src/entities/base/service.hpp" line="215" column="24" bodyfile="src/entities/base/service.hpp" bodystart="215" bodyend="223"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> for service/organisation tables (clinics, pharmacies, laboratories, ...). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Adds builders that mutate the JSONB &quot;staff&quot; array of a service row to add or remove a nominee, plus a static query used by <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1ae17e951f1dc80a8e4920571ebe9f3c21" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> to read a service&apos;s owner/admin/staff. CRUD statements remain inherited from <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The staff builders bind the nominee and entity ids through <ref refid="structBase_1_1Binder" kindref="compound">Binder</ref>; the static permission query interpolates the service name and id into its text and is used as a permission cache key. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="structapi_1_1v2_1_1Types_1_1StaffData" kindref="compound">api::v2::Types::StaffData</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
